/**
 * brussels.ts — the Brussels city page's data (SPEC ADDENDUM, Brussels: "band for every point, from
 * the city's own model").
 *
 * Map method: 'surface'. A MOCK BelAQI surface shades the Brussels-Capital Region, standing in for
 * IRCELINE's interpolated hourly layer (./areas/brussels-surface.json, generated by
 * ./generators/gen_brussels_surface.py). Sample data in place of the city's own model output; never
 * a surface we compute from readings. Sensor markers are neutral.
 *
 * Sources (READ BEFORE EDITING; research files under
 *   research/landscape/analysis/_data-catalogue/validation/brussels/v2/)
 *   - Index: BelAQI hourly (./indexes.ts, hourly rows of brussels-aqi-bands.csv).
 *   - Advice: brussels-health-advice.csv. Only the two items tied to BelAQI bands are shown (levels
 *     1 to 5, levels 6 to 10), general population, never reworded. The pollution-peak and heat-and-
 *     ozone plans' group advice is tied to alert thresholds and plan phases, not to a band, so it is
 *     not shown (round 3 decision E). No group headings, because Brussels ties no group to a band.
 *   - Pollutant sources: brussels-sources-of-pollutants.csv, Brussels Environment's 2024 inventory
 *     (indicator page and LRTAP raw data). Shares as published.
 *   - Population: no figure confirmed in the research files, so none is shown (rule 6).
 *   - Links: IRCELINE and Brussels Environment pages from the research files; the Breathe Cities
 *     page was checked live on 2026-10-25.
 *
 * Mock and sample (spec rule 8): the surface, the sensors (approximate positions from IRCELINE's own
 * map; locality labels and station types mock), per-pollutant levels, growth series, the blurb.
 *
 * Key exports: BRUSSELS
 * External dependencies: ./indexes, ./city-sensors, ./city-page, ./sensors/brussels-page.json,
 *   ./areas/brussels-surface.json.
 */

